<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="030" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-11 — full test suite green on net10 (unit + integration + arch)</title>
    <phase>P3 Test green + re-baseline</phase>
    <gate>021 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Test-modifying; validates the entire retarget behaviorally; ADR-038 KEEP-path rules apply.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Diagnosing net10 test failures across the suite; bounded but potentially broad root-cause work.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Whole-suite run gating P3; depends on all behavioral fixes (H1/H2) being in.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>021</deps>
    <tags>dotnet, testing, integration-test, bff-api, migration</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Run the full test suite on net10 (unit + integration + arch via `dotnet test`) and make it green: fix real net10 test failures at their root cause. No test may be excluded, skipped, or deleted to force green without a logged rationale (ADR-038). Confirm the arch tests (`Spaarke.ArchTests`, incl. the ADR-002 plugin-size/thin-plugin checks) pass, and run the Dataverse seam integration test deferred from task 003.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in xUnit, integration-test harnesses, ArchTests, and diagnosing runtime/behavioral test failures on a new framework. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`dotnet test` is green across unit + integration + arch on net10; the Dataverse seam integration test passes (FR-03 proof); any test change is a real fix (not an exclusion) or carries a logged rationale in `notes/test-green.md`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design §8 P3 + spec FR-11. Tests move with their code (ADR-038). `TimeProvider` has no net9/10 break. The two-pass CI runner (`classify-and-retry.ps1`) + `.reliability-registry.json` exist — respect the reliability registry rather than fighting flakes. The Dataverse seam integration test is FR-03's acceptance proof, deferred here from task 003.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">tests/** (fixes where net10 surfaces a real failure)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/** (ADR compliance tests incl. ADR-002 plugin checks)</file>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/test-green.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="021" status="pending">H1/H2 behavioral fixes verified — the code under test is final.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Integration-heavy pyramid; the 7 KEEP-path categories require same-PR replacement on deletion. Coverage is observation, never a gate. Do NOT exclude/skip/delete a test to force green without a logged rationale.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01">A test that fails because behavior actually changed is a DEFECT to investigate, not a test to update — a zero-behavior-change migration should keep behavioral assertions valid (except the FR-06 telemetry carve-out).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">The arch tests enforcing thin-plugin/plugin-size MUST stay green — the net462 plugin is unchanged.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Full test-suite green on net10</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>tests/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="two-pass-runner" location="scripts/ci/classify-and-retry.ps1">CI reliability classifier + retry; respect `.reliability-registry.json`.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-11 + ADR-038. Declare RIGOR: FULL.</step>
    <step order="1">Run `dotnet test` for the full solution on net10; capture failures.</step>
    <step order="2">Triage each failure: real net10 behavioral change (investigate as a possible NFR-01 defect) vs test-harness/runtime-tied issue (fix the harness).</step>
    <step order="3">Fix at root cause; if a test genuinely must change/skip, log the rationale in `notes/test-green.md` (per ADR-038).</step>
    <step order="4">Run the Dataverse seam integration test (FR-03 proof); confirm arch tests (incl. ADR-002 plugin checks) pass.</step>
    <step order="5">Re-run until green; record the final result + any logged rationale.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 030 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a test fails because product behavior genuinely changed under net10 (beyond the FR-06 telemetry carve-out), STOP and surface per CLAUDE.md §6.5 — that violates NFR-01 and is a defect decision, not a test edit.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Run the full test suite</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/** (net10 fixes)</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/test-green.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet test` is green across unit + integration + arch on net10.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Dataverse seam integration test passes (FR-03 proof) and the ADR-002 arch tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No test was excluded/skipped/deleted without a logged rationale in `notes/test-green.md`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no test failure was "fixed" by weakening an assertion that guards zero-behavior-change.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-11. `/test-diet` reconciliation of tests added/modified happens at wrap-up (task 090).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
